{
  "_comment": [
    "SHARED FIXTURE - identical bytes in all four frameworks.",
    "  tina4-python/tests/fixtures/dotenv_corpus.json",
    "  tina4-php/tests/fixtures/dotenv_corpus.json",
    "  tina4-ruby/spec/fixtures/dotenv_corpus.json",
    "  tina4-nodejs/test/fixtures/dotenv_corpus.json",
    "",
    "One answer key for feature 1 of the feature audit (the .env parser).",
    "",
    "The .env CONTENT lives here too, as `env_file`, rather than in a sibling",
    "file. One file means one thing to keep in sync: a fixture whose input and",
    "expectations can drift apart is not an answer key. Each suite writes it to a",
    "temp directory and loads it for real - a .env is a file, so the real",
    "dependency is trivially available and there is nothing to mock.",
    "",
    "Three of these lines were silent bugs in Ruby before this row: an export",
    "prefix dropped the variable entirely, a trailing comment stayed in the value,",
    "and ${VAR} never expanded anywhere but PHP.",
    "",
    "The legacy top-level env_file/expected fields remain temporarily because the",
    "current 3.13 runners consume them. contract_3_14 is the decision-complete",
    "answer key from the 2026-08-09 adversarial audit. Runners move to that section",
    "only during the post-audit implementation phase; fixture data lands now so the",
    "contract cannot drift back into prose."
  ],
  "env_file": "PLAIN=hello\nexport EXPORTED=shellstyle\nQUOTED=\"double quoted\"\nSINGLE='single quoted'\nHOST=example.com\nINTERP=${HOST}/api\nDQ_INTERP=\"${HOST}/v2\"\nLITERAL='${HOST}/api'\nWITH_HASH=value # trailing comment\nQUOTED_HASH=\"a # b\"\nUNKNOWN=${NOPE}/x\nEMPTY=\nESCAPES=\"line1\\nline2\\ttabbed\"\nSPACED_KEY = spaced\nno_equals_sign\n1BAD=invalid key\nDQ_THEN_COMMENT=\"s3cret\" # the database password\nSQ_THEN_COMMENT='lit' # note\nTRAILING_BS=hello\\\nCONT_NEXT=world\n",
  "expected": {
    "PLAIN": "hello",
    "EXPORTED": "shellstyle",
    "QUOTED": "double quoted",
    "SINGLE": "single quoted",
    "HOST": "example.com",
    "INTERP": "example.com/api",
    "DQ_INTERP": "example.com/v2",
    "LITERAL": "${HOST}/api",
    "WITH_HASH": "value",
    "QUOTED_HASH": "a # b",
    "UNKNOWN": "${NOPE}/x",
    "EMPTY": "",
    "ESCAPES": "line1\nline2\ttabbed",
    "SPACED_KEY": "spaced",
    "DQ_THEN_COMMENT": "s3cret",
    "SQ_THEN_COMMENT": "lit",
    "TRAILING_BS": "hello\\",
    "CONT_NEXT": "world"
  },
  "_never_set": {
    "_note": "Keys that must NOT exist after loading. A malformed line is skipped with a warning, never guessed at, and one bad line never stops the rest of the file.",
    "keys": [
      "no_equals_sign",
      "1BAD"
    ]
  },
  "_rules": {
    "export_prefix": "A shell-style `export FOO=bar` is valid input. Ruby dropped these lines entirely and said nothing, so a .env copied out of a shell profile lost keys and the failure surfaced somewhere unrelated.",
    "trailing_comment": "An unquoted value ends at the first SPACE-HASH. Ruby kept the whole line, so `value # note` became 'value # note' - a wrong value rather than an absent one, which is the harder kind to notice.",
    "quoted_hash": "A `#` inside quotes is part of the value, not a comment.",
    "interpolation": "${VAR} expands in unquoted and double-quoted values against keys already loaded plus the real environment. It was PHP-only, so a .env written against PHP produced a broken literal in the other three.",
    "single_quotes_are_verbatim": "No escapes, no expansion. This is the documented way to keep a literal ${...} and the migration path for the breaking half of the change.",
    "unresolved_reference": "Left LITERAL and warned about once per name, never resolved to an empty string. PHP emptied it, so `URL=${DB_HOST}/db` with a typo silently became '/db'.",
    "empty_value": "`EMPTY=` sets the empty string. It does not unset and it is not absent.",
    "escapes": "A double-quoted value processes \\n, \\t and \\\\. A single-quoted one does not.",
    "spaced_key": "Whitespace around the key is trimmed.",
    "no_line_continuation": "A trailing backslash does NOT join the next line. The value keeps the literal backslash and the following line is parsed on its own. Node alone implemented shell-style continuation, so one .env produced a DIFFERENT SET OF VARIABLES on Node than on the other three - the swap in ADR-0024 broken at the config layer itself. The continuation loop was deleted rather than ported: no mainstream dotenv (motdotla, vlucas/phpdotenv, bkeepers/dotenv, python-dotenv) joins lines this way, so porting it to three frameworks would have moved all four off the ecosystem contract to preserve one framework's extension.",
    "quoted_then_comment": "A QUOTED value ends at its CLOSING QUOTE; anything after it is a comment and is discarded. This corpus already covered a `#` INSIDE quotes (quoted_hash) and a `#` after an UNQUOTED value (trailing_comment), but never the case between them - and that is the single most common line in a real .env. Python, Ruby and Node decided 'is this quoted?' by testing the FIRST and LAST character, so a trailing comment made the last character non-quote, the value fell to the unquoted branch, and the QUOTE CHARACTERS were left in the value: PW=\"s3cret\" # comment yielded the 8-character string \"s3cret\" including quotes. A credential handed to a driver with quotes baked into it. PHP was correct - it scans for the closing quote. Missing corpus row, not a missing fixture: all four passed this file byte-identically while 3 of 4 were wrong."
  },
  "truthiness": {
    "_note": "The ONE env truthiness table. Every env boolean, in every framework, in every subsystem, answers from this set. It was NOT one table: Ruby's Env.bool also accepted y/t/n/f while Ruby's OWN Log and Mcp checks did not, so TINA4_LOG_FUNC=y turned function logging ON while TINA4_DEBUG=y left debug OFF - same process, same .env, two answers. Single letters were dropped rather than spread to the other three: systemd's boolean set is 1/yes/true/on with no letters, and YAML 1.2 removed y/n precisely because a bare letter reads as a value (the Norway problem). Comparison is case-insensitive after stripping surrounding whitespace.",
    "truthy": ["true", "TRUE", "True", "  true  ", "1", "yes", "YES", "on", "ON"],
    "falsy": ["false", "FALSE", "0", "no", "off", "", "   ", "y", "t", "n", "f", "Y", "T", "maybe", "2", "-1", "truthy", "onwards"]
  },
  "precedence": {
    "_note": "real environment > .env.local > .env, first-wins. A stray gitignored .env.local must never clobber an explicitly-set production variable.",
    "env": "PRECEDENCE_KEY=from_env\nSHARED_KEY=from_env\n",
    "env_local": "PRECEDENCE_KEY=from_env_local\n",
    "expected_without_real_env": {
      "PRECEDENCE_KEY": "from_env_local",
      "SHARED_KEY": "from_env"
    },
    "real_env_wins": {
      "key": "PRECEDENCE_KEY",
      "value": "from_real_environment"
    }
  },
  "contract_3_14": {
    "status": "decision-complete; implementation and runner wiring wait for the full audit",
    "contract": "tina4-documentation/plan/v3/features/001-dotenv.md",
    "schema": {
      "given": "real filesystem sources plus pre-load environment, initialized framework constants, target and override mode",
      "when": "one public DotEnv operation",
      "then": "native return, raw process values, filesystem effects, error details and reset state",
      "error": "category=configuration; every hard failure is transactional",
      "native_types": ["string", "boolean", "null", "integer", "float", "sequence", "map"]
    },
    "canonical_template": "# Tina4 project settings\nPROJECT_NAME=\"My Project\"\nTINA4_DEBUG=true\nTINA4_LOCALE=en\nTINA4_LOG_LEVEL=ALL\nTINA4_SWAGGER_ENABLED=false\nTINA4_SWAGGER_VERSION=1.0.0\nTINA4_SWAGGER_DESCRIPTION=\"Edit your .env file to change this description\"\n",
    "cases": [
      {
        "id": "ENV-T01",
        "given": {"target": "$ROOT", "files": {}},
        "when": {"operation": "load_env"},
        "then": {"created": {".env": "$canonical_template"}, "not_created": [".env.local"], "native": {"PROJECT_NAME": "My Project", "TINA4_DEBUG": true, "TINA4_LOCALE": "en", "TINA4_LOG_LEVEL": "ALL", "TINA4_SWAGGER_ENABLED": false, "TINA4_SWAGGER_VERSION": "1.0.0", "TINA4_SWAGGER_DESCRIPTION": "Edit your .env file to change this description"}, "credentials_created": false},
        "witness": "bootstrap_exact_bytes_and_no_credentials"
      },
      {
        "id": "ENV-T02",
        "given": {"target": "$ROOT", "files": {".env": "VALUE=1\n"}},
        "when": {"operation": "load_env"},
        "then": {"files_unchanged": [".env"], "native": {"VALUE": 1}, "process": {"VALUE": "1"}},
        "witness": "existing_main_never_rewritten"
      },
      {
        "id": "ENV-T03",
        "given": {"target": "$ROOT/missing.env", "files": {}, "environment": {"KEEP": "before"}},
        "when": {"operation": "load_env"},
        "then": {"error": {"category": "configuration", "path": "$ROOT/missing.env", "reason": "missing explicit file"}, "environment": {"KEEP": "before"}, "created": []},
        "witness": "missing_explicit_file_hard_fails"
      },
      {
        "id": "ENV-T04",
        "given": {"target": "$ROOT", "filesystem": "bootstrap-write-denied", "environment": {"KEEP": "before"}},
        "when": {"operation": "load_env"},
        "then": {"error": {"category": "configuration", "path": "$ROOT/.env", "reason": "write failure"}, "environment": {"KEEP": "before"}},
        "witness": "bootstrap_failure_is_not_empty_success"
      },
      {
        "id": "ENV-T05",
        "given": {"target": null, "project_root": "$ROOT", "environment": {"TINA4_ENV_FILE": "config/app.env"}, "files": {"config/app.env": "VALUE=main\n", "config/.env.local": "VALUE=local\n"}},
        "when": {"operation": "load_env"},
        "then": {"native": {"VALUE": "local"}, "resolved_main": "$ROOT/config/app.env"},
        "witness": "selector_relative_resolution_and_local_sibling"
      },
      {
        "id": "ENV-T06",
        "given": {"target": "$ROOT/config/app.env", "files": {"config/app.env": "VALUE=main\n", "config/.env.local": "VALUE=local\n"}},
        "when": {"operation": "load_env"},
        "then": {"native": {"VALUE": "main"}, "sources_read": ["config/app.env"]},
        "witness": "explicit_file_has_no_implicit_sibling"
      },
      {
        "id": "ENV-T07",
        "given": {"target": "$ROOT", "files": {}, "concurrency": 2},
        "when": {"operation": "load_env_concurrently"},
        "then": {"created_once": ".env", "content": "$canonical_template", "partial_reads": 0, "truncations": 0},
        "witness": "exclusive_atomic_bootstrap"
      },
      {
        "id": "ENV-P01",
        "given": {"target": "$ROOT", "override": false, "environment": {"VALUE": "ambient"}, "files": {".env.local": "VALUE=local\nLOCAL_ONLY=local\n", ".env": "VALUE=main\nLOCAL_ONLY=main\nMAIN_ONLY=main\n"}},
        "when": {"operation": "load_env"},
        "then": {"native": {"VALUE": "ambient", "LOCAL_ONLY": "local", "MAIN_ONLY": "main"}, "process": {"VALUE": "ambient", "LOCAL_ONLY": "local", "MAIN_ONLY": "main"}},
        "witness": "ambient_local_main_precedence"
      },
      {
        "id": "ENV-P02",
        "given": {"target": "$ROOT", "override": true, "environment": {"VALUE": "ambient"}, "files": {".env.local": "VALUE=local\n", ".env": "VALUE=main\n"}},
        "when": {"operation": "load_env"},
        "then": {"native": {"VALUE": "local"}, "process": {"VALUE": "local"}},
        "witness": "override_never_reverses_file_precedence"
      },
      {
        "id": "ENV-P03",
        "given": {"target": "$ROOT", "files": {".env": "VALUE=first\nVALUE=second\n"}, "environment": {"KEEP": "before"}},
        "when": {"operation": "load_env"},
        "then": {"error": {"category": "configuration", "lines": [1, 2], "reason": "duplicate assignment"}, "environment": {"KEEP": "before"}, "absent": ["VALUE"]},
        "witness": "same_file_duplicate_hard_fails"
      },
      {
        "id": "ENV-P04",
        "given": {"target": "$ROOT", "files": {".env.local": "VALUE=local\n", ".env": "VALUE=main\n"}},
        "when": {"operation": "load_env"},
        "then": {"native": {"VALUE": "local"}, "error": null},
        "witness": "cross_file_collision_is_precedence_not_duplicate"
      },
      {
        "id": "ENV-P05",
        "given": {"target": "$ROOT", "files": {".env.local": "URL=http://${HOST}/api\n", ".env": "HOST=localhost\n"}},
        "when": {"operation": "load_env"},
        "then": {"native": {"URL": "http://localhost/api", "HOST": "localhost"}},
        "witness": "cross_file_dependency_graph"
      },
      {
